A||||3||isthiswhereiputausername?||possible to keep both power & manual locks in fiero doors?||||1||
Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-26-2001||03:07 PM||||Never ripped mine apart yet, but wondering if there is enough room to put a motor in there without conflicting with anything else..?<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||08-26-2001||03:33 PM||||Power locks don't interfere with manual locks. Even cars with power locks still have the manual slider on them. <P>Is that what you were asking?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||08-26-2001||03:35 PM||||Yes.  The manual lock is retained when you add the power locks.  The power lock actuator just attaches to the lock rod that is already in the car.  It's just that instead of pulling the lever back and forth, the power lock actuator does it for you.<P>||||reg||1
